### Test Migration Cancellation Flow
### This file demonstrates how to test the migration cancellation functionality

### 1. Start a Migration (replace with your actual migration request)
POST http://localhost:7071/api/migrations/start
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceStore": {
    "storeId": "test-store",
    "apiUrl": "https://api.bigcommerce.com/stores/test-store/v3",
    "apiKey": "your-api-key"
  },
  "destinationStore": {
    "storeId": "dest-store", 
    "apiUrl": "https://api.bigcommerce.com/stores/dest-store/v3",
    "apiKey": "your-dest-api-key"
  },
  "entities": ["categories", "products"],
  "settings": {
    "batchSize": 10,
    "enableLogging": true
  }
}

### 2. Get Migration Status (use the migrationId from step 1)
GET http://localhost:7071/api/migrations/{{migrationId}}/status

### 3. Cancel the Migration (while it's running)
POST http://localhost:7071/api/migrations/{{migrationId}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

### 4. Verify Cancellation Status
GET http://localhost:7071/api/migrations/{{migrationId}}/status

### 5. Check Migration Details
GET http://localhost:7071/api/migrations/{{migrationId}}

### Expected Results:
# Step 1: Should return migrationId and status "Queued" or "InProgress"
# Step 2: Should show migration status as "InProgress" 
# Step 3: Should return status "cancelled" with cancellation timestamp
# Step 4: Should show migration status as "Cancelled"
# Step 5: Should show full migration details with cancellation info

### Test Edge Cases:

### Try to cancel a non-existent migration
POST http://localhost:7071/api/migrations/non-existent-id/cancel

### Try to cancel an already completed migration
POST http://localhost:7071/api/migrations/completed-migration-id/cancel

### Try to cancel an already cancelled migration  
POST http://localhost:7071/api/migrations/cancelled-migration-id/cancel 